  "text": "Forsyth County - Board of Elections\nHome\nBoard of Elections\nAbout\n2026 Board Meeting Schedule\nBoard Meeting Minutes\nBoard Resolutions\nElection Academy\nVoter Resources\nPolling Places\nProvisional Voting\nVoter Registration\nFrequently Asked Questions\nAbsentee & Early Voting\nAbsentee By-Mail Voting\nEarly Voting\nMultipartisan Assistance Team (MAT)\nCandidates\nCandidates & Filing Information\nCampaign Finance Report\nElection Resources\nElection Information\nVoter Data\nElection Workers\nSearch through site content\n\u00d7\nEarly Voting Locations and Wait Times\nVoting early? Check the current wait times before you head to the polls!\nView current early voting location wait times.\n\u00d7\nPhoto ID Requirements\nA Photo ID is required for voting. Be prepared for upcoming elections and have your ID ready.\nLearn more about Photo ID requirements\n\u00d7\nNC Registration Repair Project\nClick here to learn more about the state's ongoing efforts to collect missing identification numbers from certain voters.\nLearn more about the NC Registration Repair Project\nAm I Registered?\nAm I Registered?\nRegister to Vote\nRegister to Vote\nAbsentee by Mail Voting\nAbsentee by Mail Voting\nEarly Voting\nEarly Voting\nSample Ballot\nSample Ballot\nFind My Polling Place\nFind My Polling Place\nList of Candidates\nList of Candidates\nElections Schedule\nElections Schedule\nElections Worker Application\nElections Worker Application\nFind My Elected Representatives\nFind My Elected Representatives\nE-Notification Sign Up\nE-Notification Sign Up\nElection Results\nElection Results\nLatest News\n9/17/2026\nOfficial Summary Explanation of 2026 Constitutional Amendments\n8/28/2026\nUpdated UOCAVA Notice For The November 3, 2026 General Election\n8/25/2026\nSCHEDULE OF ABSENTEE MEETINGS FOR THE NOVEMBER 3, 2026 GENERAL ELECTION\n2/12/2026\nFAQ: Letters to Voters About Unvalidated ID Numbers\nView Archived News\nElections Director\nTim Tsujii, Elections Director\nUseful Links\nState Board of Elections\nN.C. General Assembly\nFederal Election Commission\nU.S. Election Assistance Commission\nContact Us\nForsyth County Government Center\n201 North Chestnut Street\nWinston-Salem, NC 27101\nPhone: 336 703 2800\nFax: 336 727 2893\nEmail:\nContact Us\nHours of operation: 8am-5pm Monday-Friday\nConnect with us:\nView this profile on Instagram\nForsythBOE\n(@\nfcvotes\n) \u2022 Instagram photos and videos\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Forsyth County, North Carolina.\nAccessibility\nScroll To Top",
